WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I´m great. How are you?

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good. It´s very nice
having you in the building.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s exciting to be here.
30 Rock.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were talking backstage.
A lot has changed.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.775 size:75% position:38%
You went from a show
that was on at night

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
to now a show
that is on in the morning,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.077
and you were saying backstage

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
you see your children
a lot more.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
That must be nice.
-Yeah, it´s amazing.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.181
I´m -- I´m having a totally
different experience with them.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve gone from, "Hurry up!
Get your backpack!

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´ve got to go!"
to "It´s almost time for bed.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on. You´ve got
to brush your teeth.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on.
Here we go."

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s great. They must be
so much more into that.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But can I tell you that
the nighttime routine

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.594
is much more rewarding
than the morning routine.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s just -- You know, like,
tucking them in...

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.363
-Oh, putting kids to bed.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...reading the stories,
doing all that.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That´s so great
that you told me

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
the thing I miss every night,
doing this show is the --

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sorry. Sorry.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.239
-Yeah. It´s really cool of you.
I thank you so much for that.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As they age up,
we´ll get more time.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Voice breaking ]
God damn it, Megyn.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m sorry.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn´t need
to go through this tonight.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.012
-There´s always FaceTime.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.681
-[ Normal voice ] There´s other
changes from night to morning.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´ve noticed,
in the very few short weeks

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.152
you´ve been doing your show,

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
there´s a lot more to do
in a morning show.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.189
-You know, I´ve been amazed at
how much I have to move around.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I used to be able
to just sit at the desk

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
and look into the camera
and deliver the news.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now it´s like --
I don´t know.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
There´s, like, dried smoke
coming into the studio

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got to walk down,
like, a runway,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.069
and I got to -- I don´t know --
do yoga.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, so you got to do
all that stuff,

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.272 size:84% position:42%
and then you got to do
the serious interviews.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it´s the full gamut.
-Yeah.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, in that one,
I´ve got it over you,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I just move
behind a desk

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just talk about the news,
so I --

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s so nice.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you might put your kids
to bed, but sweet desk.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nailed it.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, you have --
You pointed out that you want

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
to talk about politics less
in your new job,

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I imagine
that you do not miss --

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or you can tell me.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you miss
talking to politicians?

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I really do miss
Mitch McConnell.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Desperately.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.598
I miss our time together.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He should come
on your morning show.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Anthony Weiner.
Like, I -- No.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You should make scones
with Anthony Weiner

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.736 size:75% position:38%
on the "Today" show.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um...
-As, like, a work release.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.878 size:81% position:41%
-You know, it´s one of
those things, like --

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.547
Look, if a big hurricane comes,
we´re gonna talk about it.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.216 size:81% position:41%
But we´re not gonna be
The Weather Channel.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
If something big happens
politically,

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.918
we´re gonna talk about it,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don´t want to do it
all the time

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.521 size:75% position:38%
like I did on cable.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.256
Because it´s soul-killing.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, so we´ll do it, you know,
where appropriate.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just don´t want to do it
all the time.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.462 size:78% position:39%
Talking to, you know,
with all do respect,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.930 size:81% position:41%
to those guys, it´s --

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.933 size:88% position:44%
Those are not the best
interviews, as you know.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.101
-Yeah. Well, I -- You know,

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
tell me if you´ve found
the same thing.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
I find -- And this is
across the aisle.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.641
Republicans and Democrats
do it exactly the same.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:25.411
Most politicians answer the
question they wish you´d asked.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you ask the question
you want an answer to,

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.449
and the next thing you know,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
you realize,
"Oh, this isn´t it."

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.252
-And they´ll take 12 minutes...
-Yeah.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...to answer it.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you get so bored
that you just give up.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. [ Laughs ]

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.625 size:84% position:42%
Well, that is one thing
that I would never do.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I always felt like --
and still do --

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.161
that I was there as the advocate
for the audience

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.462 size:81% position:41%
and not for the guest.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I´m -- I´m not shy
about interrupting somebody

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.267
and sort of saying, "Boring."

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that doesn´t
make the experience fulfilling

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it´s over.
-Sure.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.572 size:78% position:39%
-And they´re still --
They´re spin masters.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They are.
There´s a lot of spinning.

